#1105 is fixed and committed as e30a8964. When a fence is active, list_files no longer passes on a find warning that the output cap cut off partway through its path. A cut that ends inside a denied directory's own name (‘/home/u/.s for --deny-dir ~/.ssh) now gets withheld, with its own note saying why. The full suite passes, as do clippy with -D warnings and fmt.

How the cut is detected. I read yoagent 0.25.16's tools/list.rs and didn't guess the shape: it always appends the line ... (more warnings not shown) after the cut. So only the line directly above that marker can be cut. That line is treated as cut when its path never reaches its closing separator, which covers GNU's curly-quoted output, C-locale ' quoting and BSD's unquoted output.

What changed in the code (src/fence_result_filter.rs):
• filter_fenced now takes fence_active. That flag already existed one level up and is now passed down.
• fence_tool_error takes it too, so the case where nothing could be listed (Listing error: …) is covered as well. That needed a 4-arg call at its two call sites in tool_wrappers.rs. rustfmt splits each call onto several lines, so the file grew by 10 lines, and I updated its size entry in tests/module_size.rs (5736 → 5746).
• The existing path check still runs first, so a cut inside the denied directory (…/.ssh/ke) is still reported as a withheld result, as before.
• With no fence, the output is byte-identical to before.

Tests:
• The ticket's case in all three quoting styles, plus the error path.
• Each fixture first checks that the cut prefix really is in the input, so a test can't pass by matching nothing.
• Near-misses that must pass through unchanged: no fence; a complete warning line; a line where only the reason text after the path was cut; and the existing case of a cut inside the denied directory.
• Positive control, run as one command: I disabled the new branch, exactly the two tests for the new behaviour failed by name, then I restored it and they passed. No sabotage marker is left in the tree.

Docs:
• permissions.md has one new sentence about cut lines.
• The ARCHITECTURE.md entry for this residue is now past tense and describes the fix, plus one stated limit: a warning name that itself contains ’:  is still judged by its first segment only.
• While checking, I found the module doc still said find warnings are "kept verbatim". That has been false since #1023, so I corrected it in the same commit.
• Every #1105 reference left in src, docs and ARCHITECTURE.md describes the fixed behaviour, so none goes stale when the push closes the ticket.
